WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.187
Sometimes data arrives in separate numerical blocks that need to be combined.

00:00:05.187 --> 00:00:08.737
NumPy provides several ways to do this.

00:00:08.737 --> 00:00:12.772
Concatenate joins arrays along an existing axis.

00:00:12.772 --> 00:00:19.695
Vertical stack places arrays on top of each other, while horizontal stack places them side by side.

00:00:20.221 --> 00:00:24.213
The correct choice depends on what the rows and columns represent.

00:00:24.213 --> 00:00:31.768
For example, two batches of observations may be stacked vertically because they share the same variables.

00:00:31.768 --> 00:00:37.168
Two groups of features for the same observations may be joined horizontally.

00:00:37.168 --> 00:00:43.406
Before combining arrays, check their shapes and confirm that the dimensions are compatible.
